   },
   "title": "MiniMax H3 Fast Draft - lower detail, less GPU work",
   "widgets_values": [
    "# MiniMax H3 Fast Draft\n\n**544 x 544, four steps** - the 544p-trained Turbo LoRA in its supported four-step mode (video/audio shift 12/3), INT8 attention and Sol-Attn sparse attention. About half the pixels per frame of the 768 workflows: use it to check timing and framing, then render the final with Fast or the standard workflow.\n\n1. Upload **Portrait** and **Voiceover**.\n2. In **Talking-Head Prompt**, describe the `subject` and `background` you see in the portrait. The fields come filled in for an example portrait; rewrite them for yours and keep the leading `subject:` / `background:` tags (optional, stripped).\n3. Test one chunk (batch count 1), then queue audio seconds / 8, plus a margin. Each item renders the next unfinished chunk; the last one stitches `output/<audio name>_draft.mp4`. A new voiceover starts at chunk 1 in its own folder - nothing to reset.\n\nThe LoRA filename says 8step; four-step inference is intentional and supported by its authors.\n\nModel and sampling nodes below are collapsed: double-click to inspect them.\n\nLicence and full instructions: https://github.com/tenitsky/minimax-h3\n"
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1680,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
